Retail script SFX now arbitrate two replaceable channels. Hash-guarded static
evidence in tools/inspect-sound-slots.py establishes descriptor word zero as
the bank-local record index plus one (44cc96), preserved across lazy loading
(44ddde..44de0b). 425150 singlesound requires a strictly greater ID than the
lowest channel and suppresses an ID already in the other channel. 425240
multiplesound allows equal-ID restart and replaces the matching other channel
when present. 425330 dualsound replaces each lower-ID channel independently;
425400 bothsound replaces both unconditionally. Inactive channels have ID zero;
ties select channel 2. These comparisons deliberately use bank-local IDs, even
across banks, matching the original. Physical setup 4018c0 frees the old chain.
Native looping mixer fixtures exercise these branches and 100 repeated calls.
Audio corpus/mixer checks pass for all three editions without channel exhaustion.
The retail policy is enabled only for the supplied version-4, 95488-byte BOOTFILE,
matching the detection table's size. The September demo now has a separate
verified policy: 426440 aliases 426240, and 426450 replaces the lower channel.
Its composite bank priorities and range-entry loop arming are described below.
Dust arbitration is now verified below. Movie cue ownership remains pending.
The corrected native retail build passes all 366 actions through turbine
regulation, Rubaiyat retrieval/stash and Vlad's package request with no mixer
exhaustion. build/full-vlad-sound-slots.log and its RGBA/PNG capture record it.
tools/verify-full-turbine.ps1 now rejects mixer-slot warnings in this replay.

Loop busy checks resolve the first handler before checking reentrancy: a local
idle callback must run while an unrelated BOOT idle yields. Deferred
sendtoboot/sendtobootfx address the first BOOT
container defining the handler, with caller-evaluated arguments and recipient
context. starxyz queries named-star coordinates with axes 1..4 and packed signed
ground halves. Native prop fixtures cover independent/self-rearmed idle, BOOT
library addressing/context, all star axes and missing names. Full playthroughs
and save/load remain incomplete.
Native save/load checkpoints
---------------------------
Experimental gameplay now connects savegame/opengame, runtime save/load menus
and startup slot loading to native ScummVM saves. The original control-panel
buttons call the ScummVM chooser; the development viewer still has no saves.
DFSV version 5 is a ScummVM-owned format, not the original TI/DF save format.
It stores BOOT identity/globals, resource paths/CD/canonical sources, world
owners and runtime copies, inventory, room/stage/camera, palettes/text,
clocks/random state, scheduler, actor motion, crickets, Dust projectiles and PCM playback.
Version-1/2/3/4 checkpoints remain readable.
Audio offsets use mixer milliseconds rather than sample-accurate positions.
Conversations, movies and camera transitions are not save checkpoints; VM
stacks are not persisted. Original save import is not implemented.

Loads validate bounded fields/checksum, edition, assets and visible sprites in
a detached session before commit, without replaying open callbacks. Successful
loads abandon the previous script frames. Modal choosers resynchronize the game
clock, including cancellation. Canonical sources preserve installed/CD variants
and Dust's distinction between room filename and internal name.

tools/verify-save-state.ps1 passes cold-boot round trips, fresh-process restores,
ScummVM slots and physical input through all three authored control panels.
Nine malformed/missing-asset fixtures plus a cross-edition save reject without
changing live room/stage/time/globals, and navigation remains functional.
tools/save-fixtures.py reproduces those invalid saves. Optional -Story saves
after Sasha, completes retail mission one, rolls back to HALLA / View58 with
mission=1, phase=3, vladfood=frank and rubaiyat=coal5, and completes the remaining
route in a fresh process. Both native rollback and continuation pass; see
build/save-full-story-native.log and build/save-full-fresh-story-native.log.
The fresh route writes build/save-full-mission2.dfsv; independent restoration
passes with mission=2, phase=0, vladfood=vlad and rubaiyat=frank.

Control-panel diagnostics auto-select actual save slots; interactive chooser
QA, audible restoration, later story/puzzle checkpoints and original save
imports remain pending. This is checkpoint support, not full-playability proof.

Audio/stage/room/cast/prop regressions pass in all three editions. The room
library fixture now expects the stage's own me with the addressed scene as
target, including self-closure while its script is running. Dust's blackjack
route passes with normal speech. Escape-based diagnostic speech skipping changes
its help/jug-pickup route and is not equivalent to that normal-dialogue replay.
The complete demo route also passes after save/load integration: 306 actions,
twelve choices, phase=2 and postdemo.mov; build/save-demo-completion-native.log.

