verify-dust-handkerchief-chit.ps1 physically returns to Fearwitt and drags it
onto him, receiving degree 1. Fresh save-handkerchief-chit restoration retains
the gun, boots and day 2/clock 2/phase 0 and permits ordinary navigation without
death (build/dust-handkerchief-chit-restore-native.log). Later story remains
unfinished.


Dust afternoon trading / Cobb
----------------------------
Native replays pass the chit-to-wine exchange with Buick, wine-to-skooch exchange
with Bloodstone, and Laurel's ammunition trade, including normal modal inventory
selection. A normal $1 bank deposit leaves cash $4 / account $1 and all three
equipment items. Flippo's warning and Jones's interruption advance to phase 1.
The Chinese-store confrontation passes inventory gun selection, normal approach,
Cobb's dialogue, drawing/firing, cobbshot.mov and Dell's surrender: phase 3,
bulletcount 5, no death. Checkpoint: build/save-dust-cobb-defeated.dfsv.
Helpers: verify-dust-buick-wine, verify-dust-blood-skooch,
verify-dust-laurel-bullets, verify-dust-bank-deposit, verify-dust-flippo-alarm and
verify-dust-cobb.ps1; corresponding build/dust-*-suite.log/native.log.

Trace-only modal click sequencing now recognizes a prop selection that finishes
without yielding after its released click, allowing the next OK press. Actual
Dust trade selectors pass; Titanic's smokestack/notebook/gas-pen sequence and
fresh restoration also pass (build/modal-selection-retail-regression.log).

verify-dust-sheriff.ps1 passes the Mayor's appointment, badge handoff, Dell's
jail placement and unskipped d2ad2n.mov. save-dust-day2-night.dfsv reaches day 2 /
clock 3 / phase 0 in JAIL, badge=stranger, dell=jail, equipment retained and bank
account $1. Fresh restoration and inventory open/close pass
(build/dust-day2-night-restore-native.log). Appointment evidence:
build/dust-sheriff-suite.log and dust-sheriff-native.log. Later night events,
days 3–5 and endings remain unfinished.

Dust day-three progression and original projectile semantics (2026-10-13)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The second-night Laurel conversation, normal bed selection and unskipped
D2ND3M.MOV transition, Buick's day-three wakeup and breakfast/hairpin/meal
sequence pass native input traces. The story reaches day 3, clock 1, phase 2.
Helpers: verify-dust-night2-laurel.ps1, verify-dust-second-night.ps1,
verify-dust-day3-wakeup.ps1 and verify-dust-day3-breakfast.ps1.

Dust's opcode 12007 is makeball, not v4 makecricket. balls.cpp implements the
original 16-slot signed-word projectile table: velocity, optional gravity and
bounce, nested pause counts, lifetime, cell building tests and swept per-axis
actor/player hitboxes. Completed records are removed before endball callbacks.
The service runs after actor movement on 50 ms passes, including busy scripts.
Original hitbox argument 1 is vertical and argument 2 horizontal. The original
camera getter also differs from playerxyz: it includes setback and eye height.
Dust camerahi reads the room eye height. Titanic's existing getters and ambient
sound behavior are retained. Hash-checked read-only evidence is reproducible
with tools/inspect-dust-balls.py; no original executable is launched.

All three native audio and room audits pass. The Dust audio audit now tests
projectiles rather than claiming v1 ambience equivalence; Titanic still runs
its compiled ambient API and SDL mixer tests. Native range input hits the
water tower through an actual moving bullet, breaks six bottle/can targets,
reloads six chambers, exits with a fair score and receives Leroy's matchbox.
verify-dust-day3-range-entry.ps1 and verify-dust-range.ps1 reproduce that route.
Good/great range scores and moving-bird hits have not yet been verified.

DFSV version 2 adds the bounded projectile table and retains version-1 loading.
A real shot saved in flight restores identical position, velocity and remaining
frames, then completes normally (verify-dust-projectiles.ps1). Version-1 demo
and late retail checkpoints load, re-save as version 2 and round-trip while
preserving their story state. Broad save validation remains incomplete.

Dust's stage loader selects its first flat before openstage, then dispatches
openflat if the callback retained that file and index. Same-flat navigation
inside openstage can therefore dispatch openflat again. The original loader
at 0x415850/0x415d30 confirms this; inspect-dust-stages.py reproduces the evidence.
All three native stage lifecycle audits pass. This fixes SCORP.FLT scheduling
its drawer-opening timer for "none". The drawer now opens and accepts the earned
matchbox through a normal inventory drag. The remaining schoolhouse puzzle and
Dust story still require validation; these checks do not establish completion.

The schoolhouse scorpion puzzle now passes native input. The earned matchbox
is dragged into the drawer, left there while returning to town, and becomes
owned by the scorpion through the courtyard scene's normal openscene handler.
On revisiting, the matchbox and pages have their safe degrees; both are collected
and the drawer is closed without death. verify-dust-matchbox-in-desk.ps1 and
verify-dust-pages.ps1 reproduce the puzzle. The next morning gate still requires
returning the ring to Jones. His four-choice request conversation also passes
(verify-dust-jones-ring-story.ps1); his patrol must be approached from its visible
side rather than assuming he remains at the bone star.

The complete ring route now passes: Jones's request, Fearwitt's explanation,
Marie's return and an ordinary drag giving the ring to Jones. With the pages
collected, town navigation triggers the unskipped D3MD3A.MOV transition.
The verified checkpoint is day 3, clock 2, phase 0 (Town Scene G9 north).
verify-dust-ring-to-marie.ps1, verify-dust-ring-return.ps1,
verify-dust-ring-jones.ps1 and verify-dust-day3-afternoon.ps1 reproduce this.
The native opening and complete fair-score range/reload/reward route also pass
after the lifecycle change. All nine malformed-save fixtures pass rejection
for DFSV v2, as do checksummed duplicate-ball, invalid-presence-flag and forbidden
retail-projectile records. Rejections preserve live story state and navigation.

The third-afternoon Yunni book and flute quests pass native input. Oona gives
the book in the saloon. Doc Rodham supplies RX; showing it to Watson and reporting
his departure unlocks pharmacy mixing. Five normal ingredient buttons play their
unskipped movies and produce the exact authored recipe and medicine degree.
Doc accepts the mixture, and leaving/re-entering his office advances treatment;
Trotter gives the flute in the inner room (docphase 9). Helpers are
verify-dust-yunni-book.ps1, verify-dust-prescription.ps1,
verify-dust-prescription-watson.ps1, verify-dust-medicine.ps1 and
verify-dust-flute.ps1. The verified state is Doctor2 Scene A1 south, day 3,
clock 2, with flute and yunnibook owned. Mask collection and later story remain
unverified at this milestone.

The mansion mask route passes: Mrs. Macintosh's authored dismissal branch
opens the gate; the table apple is collected from Scene E3 north, fed to the
caged bird from D3 west, and the mask taken from E3 east. Feeding the bird avoids
the noisy Mayor interception branch, which remains untested. The entrance view
occludes the apple; this was a viewpoint issue. Trace clicks additionally refine
around small world props when the coarse sampling grid misses an opaque pixel.
This changes only diagnostic input, not the game hit tester. Stage opening also
propagates abandonment from the initial v1 openflat callback. All three stage
audits and the retail late-checkpoint regression pass after those changes.

Normal movement with all three afternoon items triggers the unskipped D3AD3N.MOV
transition. save-dust-day3-night.dfsv reaches day 3, clock 3, phase 0, Town Scene
G7 west, with mask, yunnibook and flute retained. verify-dust-mansion-entry.ps1,
verify-dust-mask.ps1 and verify-dust-day3-night.ps1 reproduce these steps.
The earned hairpin also opens the bank at night, and the safe's actual dial
accepts physical mouse arcs for 08,23,41. dust-safe-route.mjs plans those arcs
from the supplied artwork and authored limiter; it never changes VM/save data.
Safe item collection and the remaining third-night story still need validation.

The bank safe also passes item collection. The three physical dial arcs produce
08,23,41; opening plays VAULT.MOV and SAFEBOX.MOV without skipping. Two normal
movie-region clicks open the box and take its stone, preserving actionframe(1).
The verified state is Bank Scene D1 west, day 3, clock 3, phase 0, with tstone
owned. verify-dust-safe-entry.ps1 and verify-dust-tstone.ps1 reproduce this.
The route helper now accepts exact authored scene names as well as grid labels,
needed for the native "chicken" scene in the third-night Jones quest.

Third-night reconciliation, the bounty encounter and Thunderbird reward pass
native gameplay. Five hunters die through physical shots and reloads, including
the rooftop BOUNTDIE.MOV sequence; the player survives, Trotter's dialogue clears
fighton, and Mezamee gives tbird after declining poker. Actor/cast warming is
implemented from DF.EXE 0x4259b0/0x425a30/0x428680: all member sprites enter the
shared cast cache without changing pose, step or placement. All three native
cast audits pass, including malformed-art rejection and hidden-state checks.
shopwarm was pending at that milestone; its implementation is recorded below. The consolidated five-hunter regression
passes. The required third-night Buick conversation and two physical HOTBED.MOV
clicks play D3ND4M.MOV unskipped and reach day 4, clock 1, phase 0 with both
artifacts retained. Day-four combat and later story remain unverified.

Fourth-morning Fearwitt/Jones/Trotter conversations and all three Kid attack
waves now pass native input. Consolidated wave regressions cover 13 attackers,
HENCH1/HENCH2 death movies, reloads, offscreen transitions and powder kegs.
The final-wave route survives with 24 hits by firing from the southern street
before approaching the northern barrel. A close-range route separately reaches
the authored 31-hit death branch. The Kid duel also passes all five winning
responses, the scorpion distraction, three KIDDIE.MOV target clicks and the
unskipped D4AD4N.MOV transition to day 4, clock 3, phase 0. Both artifacts remain
owned. Temple puzzles, the Bloodstone confrontation and day five remain unverified.

The fourth-night tower box and fountain passage now reach HUB.SET. A missing
flat lifecycle fallback had hidden YUNNIBOX's avatar/held item: openflat and
closeflat now follow flat -> stage containment on missing/passed handlers,
preserving normal-handler precedence and callback navigation guards. Original
DF.EXE 0x416ed0 builds both contexts. All three native stage audits and the
retail notebook/gas-pen modal regression pass. The diagnostic selector also
supports stage handlers without an active puppet. The earned tstone is placed
through physical inventory selection and dragging; the fountain opens the hub.

The sundial's physical 0,0,8 alignment and east portal lead to the flute puzzle.
Modal selection, flute placement, five note buttons, unskipped FLUTE.MOV and
return narration pass; flutepuzzle=done returns to Hub Scene D7 north on the
fourth night. Snake, mine, Thunderbird and the final confrontation/ending still
require implementation or validation.

Shop warming now supports the snake chamber's internal "puzzle" name and warms
all active prop groups/copies without changing state. All three native prop
audits pass decoded-pixel, internal-name, removed-prop and malformed-art checks.
Dust's room loader now initializes visibility before callbacks, matching
DF.EXE 0x421b80; this fixes successful puzzle returns leaving the hub hidden.
All three room audits pass; flute completion was replayed and post-return
navigation verified. Snake's seven coupled rotors also pass physical drags from
the real randomized layout, followed by unskipped SNAKE.MOV and a navigable hub
return. Thunderbird, mine, final confrontation and ending remain unfinished.

The Thunderbird alignment 8,8,4,20,12 now passes physical tumbler clicks,
TUMTRAN.MOV and a navigable hub return. The mask-guided repeating mine passes
normal keys planned from the earned standx/standy globals, then mask placement
on the skeleton and unskipped SKELETON.MOV. All four puzzle flags are done and
phase advances to 1. The shaman conversation and sundial 12,4,12 reveal the
chest. Bloodstone's confrontation transfers to Thunderbird; the alternate
8,8,0,20,16 combination plays BLOODIES.MOV and D4ND5M.MOV unskipped, reaching
day 5, clock 1, phase 0 with chest owned by stranger. The corresponding
verify-dust-tbird-puzzle, verify-dust-mine-puzzle, verify-dust-shaman-chest,
verify-dust-blood-finale-entry and verify-dust-blood-finale helpers reproduce
this progression. Endings are the next validation target.

All five day-five endings now pass their distinct unskipped movies, phase 99,
credits save/restore and authored click-to-quit. Yunni also passes all eight
scrolling names panels and their wrap to panel 1. The first farewell dialogue
was unskipped; repeat traces skip speech. verify-dust-ending.ps1 reproduces
each branch, with -FullCredits selecting a complete scrolling cycle.

Normal launch now runs the authored session without a gameplay flag. Explicit
dreamfactory_viewer=true retains the developer room viewer and its audits.
verify-launch.ps1 passes all three ordinary startup paths, including retail's
waiting game/tour menu. Direction keymaps emit arrow codes with arrow/keypad
defaults; native mappedkey probes pass in all three editions. Mouse/menu/skip
bindings are inherited from ScummVM. Physical controllers remain untested.

Font loading additionally reads LiberationSans-Regular.ttf from stock fonts.dat
when no explicit or loose font is available. Dust inventory rendering passes
with only that archive and no configured font. The development build packages
the licensed loose face beside its executable for direct Windows launches.

Retail's first winning fencing bout passes five player points, the authored
postgame dialogue and fresh restoration of willie=won/fencewins=1/fencecount=1.
verify-full-fencing-win.ps1 uses only physical attacks, selecting quadrants from
read-only snapshots. Two wins for the direct ring reward and complete parry
coverage remain unverified. Other branches and broad save/load validation are
still required before the full-playability goal can be marked complete.

Ordinary launcher startup also restores real late ScummVM slots: Dust day five,
retail best-ending preparation with all four evidence items, and the demo's
developed photograph in B59. The latter was earned again through both baths.

notedialog/questiondialog now show native ScummVM modal overlays, decode
Windows-1252 script text and freeze the game clock. Real Quit controls pass No
followed by navigation, affirmative exits, and save-before-quit restoration in
all three editions. Demo Quit first returns to its own menu; the menu exit
passes all three CLOSE.MOV click regions before scripted quit. Retail tour
entry, its save/load restriction notes and canceled Quit also pass. Full tour
coverage and debug-only textdialog remain unverified/unsupported respectively.

The optional Dust checkmove plug-in now has a portable native implementation
adapted from the pinned reference's checkers.ts. It supports compulsory jumps,
chained captures, promotion before a backward king jump, legal player moves
and alpha-beta search. Handcrafted native rules and 144 independent reference
positions pass. Bolivar's Easy board is reached through authored dialogue, and
a physical first drag passes his legal reply and the player turn handoff.
Complete matches now pass an Easy win in 58 turns and a Hard loss in 20 turns,
including captures/promotion, the losing voice wait, delayed close, postgame
dialogue and fresh-process navigation. The postgame script consumes score, so
the result is asserted before that dialogue and its removal afterward. The
portrait, real slot-99 board rollback and voluntary exit also pass. Medium
matches and Hard wins remain outside this coverage. Original DLL AI
tie-breaking/search equivalence is not claimed.

machinetype returns the Windows asset target; commandkey reads the Meta modifier.
Retail's bedsit/ship/tour Help movies pass physical topic and close clicks and
return to gameplay. Dust's normal door-close handler also passes that modifier
query. All three final native script audits, including the 144-position
checkers oracle, pass after these additions.

Dust poker passes View Cards' nested button wait, fold, repeat deal, three
physical discards, a natural winning hand, payout and voluntary exit followed
by navigation. Each phase survives a fresh-process checkpoint restore. The
diagnostic modal-click cue can include a handler gate; its event source observes
button queries to respect the script's release-before-press loop.

The inherited F5 game-menu action emits EVENT_MAINMENU. Real native menu opening,
Escape cancellation, paused game clocks and mapped keypad navigation pass in
all three editions. Script and checkers reference audits also pass.

Retail's direct two-win fencing ring reward now passes physical attacks, both
mandatory second-bout conversation branches, phase advancement and return to
SqHall. The ring, victories and phase survive a fresh-process checkpoint
restore followed by navigation. Complete defensive-parry coverage remains open.

Both left and right fencing parries now pass actual mouse defense, including
fresh-process restoration of the impending attacks and successful parry state.
Correct defense retreats without scoring; the opposite defense on the same
saved attack awards the opponent a point and recenters. Diagnostic
waitpropviewany observes alternative authored views without changing them.

All four retail smokestack layouts now have native traversal evidence. Layouts
2 and 4 were naturally drawn by normal re-entry, then climbed through their
authored barriers and stairs; their top-floor checkpoints restore and navigate.
Layout 1 was replayed separately to retain its evidence; layout 3's earlier
native trace remains available. Maze globals and random state are never injected.

MetaEngine now advertises kSimpleSavesNames to match Engine's target.### files.
Without it, direct slot loads worked but the chooser searched target.s## and
could not discover saved games. No save-format change is needed. Real Save/Load
choosers pass in all three editions, through authored controls and F5: cancel,
typed names, listed metadata, load rollback and fresh-process restoration.
The default thumbnail grid also passes New Save, name-dialog cancellation and
thumbnail loading. Diagnostic GUI inputs are ordinary events; named-widget
clicks read theme geometry and never invoke widget commands directly.

Dust's Medium and Hard checkers wins now pass their distinct dialogue, score
cleanup, store return and fresh post-match restoration. The physical test
player's tie-break favors promotion and coordinated pursuit among equally
rated moves; the native rules and opponent AI are unchanged. All three
difficulty-specific win conversations and a Hard loss have native coverage.

All three tour guide movies present in this retail package pass unskipped:
Smethells' tour9, Burns' tour2 and Trask's tour8. The initial tour9 photograph
advances through an authored physical click. Narration, post-guide dialogue,
map travel, room walks/turns, doors and fresh final navigation pass. Missing
optional guide movies are still controlled by authored file-existence checks.

Native settings controls now pass persisted volume/subtitle changes in all
three editions. Dust restores an open score panel, adjusts mute/mid/max volume
and resumes town navigation. Both Titanic rotary dials restore framerate=3
after dragging; subtitle toggles and custom turn keys survive saves and control
restored navigation. Settings observations in boot tracing are read-only.

Dust and retail death screens now pass New Game, cancelled Load, late-game
recovery and fresh restored navigation. The deaths are earned through gang
fire and Vlad's automatic carrying-Rubaiyat confrontation. Retail recovery also
crosses CD resource paths while preserving all four ending evidence items.

All original loaders initialize a new room visible before callbacks, including
v4 retail TI.EXE 0x4077e5 and demo TI.EXE 0x4083c9. This fixes the demo replay's
hidden, non-navigable cabin after quitting through its control panel. Regression
fixtures cover visibility reset and an explicit hide from the opening callback;
room audits pass all editions. Detached save loading reapplies saved visibility.
The demo's unskipped replay opening, quest reset, navigation and fresh save
restore now pass. Its 20-segment tour and 13-segment trailer also complete via
their final image clicks and return to a restorable menu.

The supplied demo also passes physical darkroom mistake paths: a negative put
directly in the second bath and one left too long in the first produce spoiled
inventory photos with value=0/degree=1, retained by fresh loads. Loading an earned
pre-bath save permits a correct retry. Saving a negative in the first bath and
loading in a new process resumes its timer and permits both baths to finish;
the collected good photo retains value=1/degree=0 through another load.
Reproduce with tools/verify-demo-photo-retry.ps1.

tools/verify-demo-completion.ps1 -Spoiled passes Penny's authored acceptance of
a spoiled Conkling photo, POSTDEMO, phase 2/menu return and fresh restoration.
The original ending closes the inventory shop. The default developed-photo
route is retained. These checks required no additional production engine fix.

Positional ambience now follows the original integer square root, linear
255-step volume and folded integer bearing pan (retail TI.EXE 0x444430/0x444790,
demo 0x444cf0/0x444f90). Previously, running loops retained their starting volume
and pan. The service now updates their existing mixer handles after movement or
turning and stops a loop on radius exit. Updated play/slot descriptors preserve
the position in saves and later master-volume changes. Read-only evidence:
tools/inspect-cricket-spatial.py and build/cricket-spatial-native-evidence.log.

Audio audits pass all editions; both Titanic mixer fixtures verify same-handle
updates, exact integer volumes, diagonal/turn panning, radius exit and reentry.
tools/verify-full-ambient-position.ps1 also passes earned turbine-room navigation:
motor volume 148 with pan -54 then 74, fresh saved-loop restoration, walking to
volume 187/pan 24 and silence beyond radius. Evidence:
build/ambient-position-audit-suite.log and build/full-ambient-position-suite.log.

Timed cricket repeats now arm only in audible range, freeze outside their
room/radius and take a fresh delay on return. Looped PCM starts immediately.
Timers may expire during a previous sample; all overlapping instances follow
position changes and stop on room/radius exit. Original 0x425730 reads the loop
flag, not playback activity. Audio audits pass the new timer/overlap checks.

DFSV v3 stores the armed flag and retains v1/v2 loading (older stored countdowns
start armed). Invalid armed flags exposed partial-table cleanup through null
entries; rejection now cleans up safely without altering the live game.
tools/verify-full-ambient-timing.ps1 verifies exact fresh saved countdown,
unarmed persistence, range reentry and invalid-flag rejection in the real ship.
Legacy v1 demo upgrades/fresh loads, v2 retail loading, v3 spatial audio and
Dust's natural in-flight projectile save/load also pass. Native retail's
two-loop priority arbitration is implemented in the following milestone.
The all-edition save suite passes v3 startup/fresh/ScummVM-slot/authored-control
round trips and invalid/cross-edition rejection (ambient-v3-save-state-suite.log).

Retail now selects the two loudest eligible loops before wave-master scaling
and plays them through the original shared SFX slots using bank-local sound IDs.
Running selected loops retain their handles; unselected descriptors stop even
if script-started. Higher-priority unrelated effects can preempt a loop, which
resumes when the slot becomes available. Timed retail repeats replace their
same-sound instance through the multiple-sound arbitration path. DFSV remains v3.

Synthetic ambience audits now explicitly select retail mode, with four generated
sounds checking three-loop selection, movement, ties, missing resources, shared
descriptor stopping, effect preemption/resumption and pre-master ranking. Audio
audits pass all editions. The earned sinking-deck crowd also passes selection
among three/four audible loops, movement promotion, fresh restores and navigation:
tools/verify-full-crowd-priority.ps1, build/full-crowd-priority-suite.log.
Turbine spatial and timer/save/rejection regressions pass under the new channels.
The proposed boiler fire-loop probe was discarded because its initialization
is unreachable after BOOTFILE setupsound's unconditional exitcode.

Cricket allocation now reuses the first inactive slot, as in both supplied v4
executables, rather than appending replacements. Interior gaps remain stable;
count/index queries and service skip them. This preserves enumeration and
equal-volume priority. Existing DFSV v3 records encode empty slots without a
format change. Native API/mixer/save checks pass replacement order, gap
enumeration, gap restoration and first-free equal-volume promotion
(CRICKET SLOT PASS; ambient-slot-audit-suite.log). All three audio audits and
the real crowd/timer/fresh-load/rejection regressions pass with this change.

Dust's alternate third-night Thunderbird route passes a natural first-hand
poker win. Legal blackjack funding preserves day=3/clock=3/phase=1. Physical
betting/discard inputs produce the winning hand, Mezamee awards the previously
unowned Thunderbird, phase/mezphase advance to 2 and the saloon remains navigable.
The unused cheating-card item and Thunderbird ownership persist across a fresh
load. Two natural hand scores passed (313 and 402). No production fix was needed.
Reproduce with tools/verify-dust-night3-poker-win.ps1 -PrepareStake; combined
evidence: build/dust-night3-poker-complete-route-suite.log. The read-only hand
oracle and ordinary-wait search adapt to timing without altering cards/globals.
Earlier $8/$15 diagnostic failures were unused-choice queues, not cash limits;
the corrected one-choice betting trace passes. The $4 exit was authored lack of
funds. Full playability/fidelity work remains active.

September demo sound arbitration and DFSV v4
-------------------------------------------
Original 426440 aliases single (426240); both (426450) unconditionally replaces
the lower-priority of two physical slots, choosing slot 2 on ties. Multiple
(426340) and single compare composite descriptor IDs: bank ordinal << 16 OR
one-based record ordinal (415c1d, 44e670). Open (44cfde) renumbers descriptors;
close (44d3d0) compacts banks without renumbering. Physical slots retain copied
IDs. tools/inspect-sound-slots.py reproduces the hash-guarded original evidence.

Demo looping crickets start once on range entry and arm 0x7fffffff (444f22).
Preempted/stopped loops wait for range reentry; timed effects share the two
physical slots. Retail's separate loudest-two pass is unchanged.

DFSV v4 preserves bank priority gaps and accepts versions 1-3; legacy demo
priorities reconstruct compact bank order because old formats lack the gaps.
Native all-edition audio and save/control-panel/invalid-save suites pass, along
with retail timer preservation and malformed armed-flag rejection. Evidence:
build/demo-sound-audit-suite.log, build/demo-sound-save-state-suite.log,
build/demo-sound-retail-timer-suite.log. Full playability remains an active goal.
The developed-photo demo completion, POSTDEMO and fresh ending restore also
pass (build/demo-sound-completion-suite.log). A preserved v1 demo save upgrades
to v4 and fresh-load physical navigation passes (demo-sound-legacy-v*-native.log).

Dust original two-channel effect arbitration
-------------------------------------------
Dust single/multiple (402b90/402c80) compare composite descriptor priorities.
Dual (402d70) aliases single; both (402d80) replaces only the lower-priority
slot, choosing slot 2 on a tie. Open (403185) calls 404290 to renumber bank
descriptors; close (4033a0) preserves gaps. Active slots retain copied IDs.
tools/inspect-sound-slots.py reproduces the hash-checked original evidence.

The earlier unbounded overlapping-effect approximation is removed. DFSV stays
v4: old Dust all-zero bank bases reconstruct stored order; their recorded two
slots/speech remain, and extra bank effects are discarded. Copied IDs protect
legitimate lone zero-base bank saves from this migration. Missing banks now
return before migration accesses an incomplete bank table.

Native synthetic v1 sound banks verify arbitration, gaps, save restoration,
renumbering, copied IDs, lone zero-base banks and 100 successive replacements.
All-edition audio/save suites pass, plus old-v4 Dust migration/fresh navigation,
four malformed sound-bank rejections with live navigation, the final gang wave,
and the Yunni ending/movie/fresh credits/authored quit. Evidence is in build:
dust-sound-audit-suite.log, dust-sound-save-state-suite.log,
dust-sound-rejection-suite.log, dust-sound-legacy-*-native.log,
dust-sound-wave3-native.log and dust-sound-ending-suite.log.
Reproduce negative bank checks with tools/verify-dust-sound-save.ps1.
Movie cue ownership and bank control lifetime still need fidelity review.
Full playability remains an active goal.

Live loop changes, bank voice controls and Dust pan
-------------------------------------------------
Native loop setters (retail 425740, demo 426860, Dust 403030) propagate to
channels 0-2, including the bank voice. The underlying repeat-link update
(Dust 41d8c0) preserves the current PCM buffer when disabling repetition.
Mutable PCM streams now enable looping mid-playback and drain the current
iteration on disable, with mixer-thread access protected by a mutex. Bank
voices inherit descriptor loop/volume/pan; independent puppet clips remain
separate.

Titanic pan setters propagate live. Dust 403010 only records the pan field;
41ce90 copies 0x27 PCM descriptor bytes, excluding pan at +31, while 402ee0
computes equal channel gains. Dust's recorded pan is therefore inaudible even
on later playback. The preliminary next-play interpretation was rejected.
tools/inspect-live-sound-controls.py reproduces the hash-checked evidence.

DFSV remains v5. Draining samples that previously looped save their modulo
position and restore the nonlooping tail. Exact synthetic PCM output and native
mid-sample loop enable, active SFX/bank voice controls, disable/drain/save/load
and eventual completion pass all three editions. Audio/movie integration,
save-panel/fresh-process/rejection and real retail motor ambience also pass.
Dust's actual range/reload/matchbox reward and death-screen restart, cancelled
Load, late recovery and fresh saves pass. Evidence: build/live-controls-*-suite.log,
live-controls-{demo,full,dust}-native.log and live-controls-dust-range-native.log.
Repeated opens of the same bank and movie cue ownership remain under review.
Full playability remains an active goal.

Bank-local sound controls and DFSV v5
-----------------------------------
Loop/volume/pan settings now live in each bank's descriptors, so closing and
reopening restores native defaults and different banks' duplicate names remain
independent. Constructors initialize loop off, volume 255 and pan 128 at retail
424b3f/46/4c, demo 425cbd/425cdc/425ce2 and Dust 402617/402639/40263f.
tools/inspect-sound-slots.py reproduces the hash-checked evidence.

DFSV v5 stores per-bank controls and active effect volume/pan snapshots. Versions
1-4 migrate name-global controls to the first matching bank; hidden banks use
defaults because legacy saves have no independent controls for them. Legacy
nonpositional playback levels reconstruct their former controls. Inline clips
retain their copied levels independently of subsequent bank/name resolution.

Native all-edition audio, movie/audio integration, save-panel/fresh-process and
invalid/cross-edition save tests pass. Synthetic native checks include hidden
duplicate names, reopen defaults, active volume/pan restoration and copied
playback levels. Preserved demo v1 and Dust v4 saves upgrade to v5/fresh navigate.
Six malformed-bank/control cases preserve live navigation; retail timer/range
and invalid armed-flag checks also pass. Real turbine movement, turning, saved
live position and radius exit pass (bank-controls-retail-position-suite.log).
Evidence: build/bank-controls-*-suite.log
and bank-controls-legacy-*-native.log. Live control propagation is verified in
the section above. Repeated opens and movie bed/theme sharing remain under
review; movie cue ownership is corrected below.
Full playability remains an active goal.

Movie cue shared-voice ownership and cleanup
-------------------------------------------
Original cues select physical voice channel 0 (retail 44ad62, demo 44b40b,
Dust 419551/4195d8). Cleanup stops it at segment/movie exits (449323, 449b41,
419362), even on natural completion. The retained-tail/effect-channel policy
was incorrect. Movie cues now replace prior voice and preserve both effects;
voice-wait frames observe the shared voice. Missing cues preserve voice/follow
state and never fall back to a sound bank. Retail implements cue loop flags
in preload/lazy paths; the September demo does not. Evidence is reproduced by
tools/inspect-movie-audio.py, guarded by original executable hashes.

Native all-edition movie/audio tests pass, including effect preservation, prior
voice replacement, missing cue/follow behavior, global voice waits, edition loop
flags and segment/natural cleanup. Fixtures explicitly assert the retail policy.
DFSV stays v5; loading keeps the current engine's edition rules rather than an
old saved policy flag. Synthetic compatibility and all-edition save-panel,
fresh-process, invalid/cross-edition and six malformed bank/control cases pass.

Actual retail best ending (four evidence items, LEAVE/DEBRIS/PROZAC, 14 credits
clicks, script quit), Dust Yunni ending/fresh credits/quit, and demo developed
photo completion/POSTDEMO/fresh restore pass. Demo tour/trailer final clicks,
menu returns and fresh restores pass; their supplied cue records lack loop flags.
Evidence: build/movie-voice-*-suite.log and movie-voice-*-native.log. Discarded
shared-loop assumptions are labelled movie-voice-unverified-loopflag-*-native.log.
Movie bed/theme sharing and repeated opens of the same bank remain under review.
Full playability remains an active goal.

PCM main-thread ownership and theme queue findings
------------------------------------------------
PCM streams borrow immutable clips and loop controls; plays, bank themes, movie
beds and restored states retain them on the main thread until mixer stop.
Mixer-thread stream destruction no longer changes non-atomic Common::SharedPtr
reference counts. The raw-pointer API states this contract; loop flags still
use their mutex. Native 256-short-clip caller-release/completion/replacement
stress checks pass per edition, along with all-edition audio/movie/save-panel,
fresh-process and invalid/cross-edition suites. Evidence:
build/pcm-ownership-{audit,movie,save}-suite.log.

Original movie beds share theme channel 3. Dust 41d040 appends submitted buffers
to an active theme chain. The initial previous-bed count is minus one (retail
448b65, Dust 418c73), so first-bed submission does not clear existing game music.
Later empty-bed segments inherit; later new-bed segments clear previous movie
music. Final cleanup stops theme only when a bed exists. Reproduce this evidence
with tools/inspect-movie-theme.py (build/movie-theme-original-evidence.log).

The separate movie mixer/immediate bank-theme replacement still needs a shared
queued theme stream and pending-buffer save restoration. A simple music stop
at movie entry would be incorrect. Queue integration and repeated bank opens
remain unfinished; full playability remains an active goal.

Authored movie soundtrack order
------------------------------
Dust beds use their explicit header directory: records after preloaded
one-shots, followed in the order at 2110 (original 418e0c..418f21). Reordered
and repeated chunks survive; unrelated unused audio is excluded. Interactive
v4 playback also preserves repeats instead of deduplicating them.

All-edition native movie suites pass (22 demo, 278 retail, 235 Dust movies),
including authored-repeat/unrelated-audio/malformed-directory fixtures and
interactive v4 playback. Evidence: build/movie-order-audit-suite.log and
build/movie-order-*-native.log. Every supplied authored bed remains within PCM
join bounds (build/movie-order-bounds.log).

Repeat boundaries (Dust header 2238; v4 table 0) are still pending together
with the shared theme queue. Original Dust 4207d0..420841 ingests pending
nodes in order and uses the last marked node as the repeat root; reproduce
with tools/inspect-movie-theme.py. The full-playability goal remains active.

Actual-data Dust Yunni ending/fresh credits/quit and demo complete tour/trailer/
final clicks/menu returns/fresh restores also pass:
build/movie-order-dust-ending-suite.log, build/movie-order-demo-media-suite.log.
Repeat-boundary and shared-channel behavior remain unfinished.

Shared queued theme channel and DFSV v6
--------------------------------------
Bank themes and movie beds share one Music mixer handle. Submissions append
their ordered chunks and select the repeat root. Dust movie header 2238 and
v4 table 0 supply it; v4 retains the original record-count clamp. Dust banks
use header+30 order and repeat from its first entry (403308..40335f). Mixed-rate
PCM keeps a fractional source cursor; repeated chunks share immutable owners.
Only the main thread prunes consumed owners, and closing a consumed old bank
preserves newer music. The mixer borrows the mutex-protected queue state.

First movie beds queue behind game music. Later empty segments inherit, new
beds replace, and final cleanup clears theme only when the film supplied a bed.
Silent movies preserve music. DFSV v6 saves pending chunks, repeat root, cursor
and a deduplicated PCM pool with bounded validation; v1-v5 themes upgrade.
tools/inspect-movie-theme.py reproduces hash-checked order/queue evidence.

The original wavevolume() sets Windows device volume, including mixed music.
Music now combines that master with relative theme gain inside ScummVM, without
changing device settings. tools/inspect-wave-volume.py resolves the actual
waveOutSetVolume imports and hash-checked callers in all editions; evidence:
build/wave-volume-original-evidence.log. This corrects the reference's separate
sound/voice-only master approximation.

Final all-edition audio/movie/native save-panel/fresh-process/invalid-save
suites pass: build/theme-master-gain-{audio,movie,save}-suite.log. Shared-queue
story replays pass retail best ending/all credits/script quit, Dust Yunni/
fresh credits/quit, demo developed-photo ending and complete tour/trailer/menu
restores: build/theme-queue-{retail-ending,dust-ending,demo-completion,demo-media}-suite.log.
These story replays precede the final volume-only correction, covered by the
final native fixtures and saves. Repeated bank opens and per-bank theme controls
still need review; the full-playability goal remains active.

Fresh opening checkpoints are v6 in all editions. Six v6 Dust sound-bank/control
rejections preserve navigation: build/theme-master-gain-dust-rejection-suite.log.

Independent bank ownership and DFSV v7
------------------------------------
Repeated opens allocate separate banks; lookup/close selects the first match.
Active effects/voices and queued themes retain owner IDs rather than filenames.
Theme gain belongs to each bank (initial 255; zero getter for banks without
music), and inactive-bank changes preserve the physical theme gain. Playback
uses bank gain rather than an unsolicited global themevolume fallback.
Track enumeration includes effects-only banks and repeats and returns internal
names, as retail CTL.STG's closetracks requires. Hash-checked original evidence:
tools/inspect-bank-controls.py, build/bank-controls-original-evidence.log.

DFSV v7 stores bank IDs/gains and play/theme/queue owner references. Validation
rejects duplicate IDs, missing owners and out-of-range gains before commit.
v1-v6 owner names and theme maps migrate. Checkpoint tools accept v7.

All-edition audio suites pass compiled script getter/enumeration checks,
independent bank defaults, inactive gains, first close, hidden instances,
nonordinal owners across saves, five malformed owner and eight malformed queue
saves: build/bank-enumeration-audio-suite.log. Movie and native/authored save
panel/fresh-process/rejection suites pass: build/bank-owners-{movie,save}-suite.log.
Six v7 Dust bank/control rejections preserve live navigation:
build/bank-owners-dust-rejection-suite.log.

Current-build retail best ending/credits/quit, Dust Yunni/fresh credits/quit,
demo developed-photo ending and complete tour/trailer/menu restores pass:
build/bank-owners-{retail-ending,dust-ending,demo-completion,demo-media}-suite.log.
Physical controls and fresh v7 settings also pass all editions:
build/bank-owners-settings-suite.log. Goal completion remains unproven; next
review includes Dust's one-shot directory, which still exposes music records.

Dust one-shot directory and DFSV v8
---------------------------------
Only header+24 one-shot records enter named sound lookup. Music remains in the
theme directory. Enumeration retains duplicate records, while named lookup
selects the first (original 404070), correcting UNILIB's duplicate pageturn.
tools/inspect-bank-controls.py reproduces original separate arrays/count/index/
first-match evidence. Corpus: 46 preserved SND variants, 17 with music,
145 music entries, duplicate pageturn in installed/CD UNILIB copies; no supplied
Titanic duplicate one-shots. Counts include preserved copies.

DFSV v8 has v7's payload layout but strict current-directory validation. Older
saves drop retired music effect controls/plays while preserving world state,
legitimate voice and queued theme. This also releases obsolete high-priority
looping effects. New retired/unknown controls reject transactionally. Native
synthetic compiled count/index/first-match, v7 cleanup, preserved state and v8
resave checks pass, together with all-edition audio/save-panel/fresh-process/
invalid/cross-edition suites: build/dust-directory-final-{audio,save}-suite.log.

Actual final gang wave, Yunni ending/fresh v8 credits/script quit also pass:
build/dust-directory-gang-suite.log, build/dust-directory-ending-suite.log.
The broader completion audit and full-playability goal remain active.

Fresh opening checkpoints are v8 in all editions; six v8 bank/control rejections
preserve navigation: build/dust-directory-rejection-suite.log.

Completion validation, 14 October 2026
------------------------------------
Fresh-start checkpoint ancestry now passes for all three supplied editions on
executable 0AB6CD9A8B06D8B6D8E8EBFCCCFA796773504D1FE2A11E4F85BDE43AB7D62027:
retail's best ending/credits/quit (57 traces), the September 1996 demo's
developed-photo completion/fresh restore (2), and Dust's five-day Yunni route
through both fights, duel, four temples, Bloodstone and credits quit (330).
The final Dust manifest is build/dust-walkthrough/20261014-121819-988/manifest.json.
Native traces use player inputs and earned saves, without injecting story,
inventory, actor damage or RNG state. Bounty and first-wave Kid spawns are
random: distant walkers legitimately clear damage in authored makemove(), so
combat verification approaches them before shooting. Temporary diagnostics
were removed before completion; production code matches the retail-run source.
All four smokestack layouts have traversal coverage; final-build 1/3/4 fresh
restores close the variant audit. Component, controls, alternate-ending and
historical optional-game evidence supplement these completion chains.
See build/completion-requirements.json for the ten verified requirements and
their scope. This supersedes earlier incomplete milestone notes above; the
engine remains experimental, with the edition/save boundaries stated at top.

Platform preparation and shared subtitle preferences
--------------------------------------------------
The subsequent Windows build integrates explicitly configured ScummVM subtitle
preferences and captions-only speech mute; without a shared override, the
authored caption switch still applies. Nine edition/mode cases, original-panel
settings/persistence and packaged fonts.dat conversation rendering pass.
The earlier 0ab completion build is preserved in build/releases/validated-0ab;
its full walkthrough evidence is historical and is not attributed to the new
settings build. See devtools/dreamfactory/README.md and
.github/workflows/dreamfactory-builds.yml for unsigned/identity-free platform
recipes, touchscreen backend controls and remaining upstream review work.
Only Windows has been built here; macOS/iOS/Android/PSP native jobs and hardware
playability remain unverified. PSP memory requirements need profiling.
